From c622c3d5398434713ea9c4e2504a5e8e0012d031 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 17:56:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] yuzu_cmd: run eden-cli with Eden Qt's config for the game

eden-cli read only its own sdl2-config.ini, so a game launched from it
ran with its defaults (keyboard controls, stock graphics) instead of the
settings tuned in Eden Qt.

When <config dir>/qt-config.ini exists, eden-cli now saves its own
config first (so no Qt value lands in it), then reads qt-config.ini as a
global config and the game's custom/<program id>.ini as a per-game
config into Settings, through the shared Config readers and SdlConfig's
player reader: every section frontend_common reads, the player
mappings, debug pad, ring controller and Qt's external_content_dirs
(kept under [UI] as Paths\external_content_dirs, as QtConfig reads it),
with each per-game value applied by its use_global flag as Eden Qt's
BootGame does. Qt's DisabledAddOns list replaces sdl2-config.ini's
instead of merging with it. The launch params are applied after both
files, so a command-line flag always wins. The reader never gets a file
path, so no save path can write the Qt files, and an absent, empty or
unreadable file, or one without the [Controls] section Eden Qt always
writes, leaves Settings as they were.
One log line names what was applied, e.g.
"Duo config: qt-config.ini + custom/0100F2C0115B6000.ini".

The program id needs a loader, so the content provider, filesystem and
factories are set up before System::Initialize instead of after the
window; the per-game values are then in place for Initialize and the
renderer pick. Without qt-config.ini, eden-cli behaves as before.

Program id 0 (homebrew) gets no per-game file; Eden Qt names that one
after the file.

Test (vibe-window host/eden-duo/test/qt_config_test.cpp, natively and
under wine): own config, qt-config.ini, then custom/<id>.ini; use_global
true and false; a per-game input profile; Qt files byte- and
mtime-identical, nothing created, no save attempted; absent, empty and
garbage files refused; external_content_dirs read from [UI]; a stale
DisabledAddOns entry dropped.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01XgyuSR8o8AbzxuWHYqLwsv
